+.. rst:directive:: .. py:type:: name
+
+   Describes a type alias. The directive can be used at module level or inside
+   a class. Its body can contain a description of the alias.
+
+   The optional ``canonical`` option describes the type represented by the
+   alias. When provided, it appears after the alias name in the signature and
+   is parsed as a type annotation, so referenced types can be cross-referenced.
+
+   .. rst:directive:option:: canonical: represented type
+      :type: Python annotation
+
+      Describe the type represented by this alias.
+
+   .. rst:directive:option:: module
+      :type: text
+
+      Describe the module containing the alias. The default is the module
+      specified by :rst:dir:`py:currentmodule`.
